  "|What ties these together is confluence : several independent signals agreeing. One signal is weak, two is suggestive, and three pointing the same way is a plan . Breakout, gap and prior-day level all agreeing is when a strategy trader acts.": "8081e81c87dce28b.mp3",
  "|What time does the US stock market's opening bell ring?": "f2b061976b59ae5e.mp3",
  "|When a candle closes its body below that higher low, the structure is broken. This is a break of structure \u2014 the first evidence the trend may be turning.": "a6c264d49b857be5.mp3",
  "|When are the MOST traders active at once?": "d8062f1cb337940d.mp3",
  "|When do you act on a reaction candle?": "d8547364deebd5c1.mp3",
  "|When does a hammer actually matter?": "645f9b021c7561d5.mp3",
  "|When highs and lows overlap with no sequence, the market is in a range . There is no structure to trade with, and the correct action is usually to wait.": "bcb2039c15a2f1ee.mp3",
  "|When price dips into a DEM/BIM for gas, how far in does it usually need to go?": "a1d009bd28e04469.mp3",
  "|When price moves decisively out of that range, that is a breakout . A break above the range high often continues up; a break below the range low often continues down. This is called the ORB \u2014 opening range breakout.": "f5464a1377ca96bf.mp3",
  "|When price reaches a goal, the method reads bodies first, wicks second . Price needs a candle body \u2014 a close \u2014 beyond the level to keep going. If only a wick pokes past and the candle fails to close there, expect it to bounce back.": "28b21ba94947a2c3.mp3",
  "|When price reaches a level, that alone is not an entry. Wait for the reaction candle to close \u2014 a bounce, a rejection, or a failed break \u2014 and only then act.": "849a4c7f36a8ca41.mp3",
  "|When price returns to a weak zone that did nothing new, the zone will not hold; price runs straight through it. The method calls this the 'Down Go Frazier' rule. Do not mark those zones.": "e5ec3fd77716815d.mp3",
  "|Which combo makes a complete trader?": "5ee69cc9879de4ec.mp3",
